{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Have you seen the [G]old man, in the [Am]closed-down [Em]market
[F]Kicking up the [C]papers, with his [F]worn-out [G]shoes?
[C]In his eyes you [G]see no pride, and [Am]there loosely [Em]at his side
[F]Yesterday's [C]paper, telling [G]yesterday's [C]news
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 1}
So [F]how can you [C]tell me, that you're mourning
[D7]And you say for you that the sun don't [G]shine?
[C]Let me take you [G]by the hand
And [Am]lead you through the [Em]streets of London
[F]I'll show you [C]something, to [G]make you change your [C]mind
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
